  "question": {
    "text": "A light cylindrical tube&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> of length <math><mi>l</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>containing air is inverted in water (density <math><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> ). One end of the tube is open and the other is closed. A block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of density <math><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is kept on the tube as shown in the figure. The tube stays in equilibrium in the position shown. Find the volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Density of the air is negligible as compared with the density of water :<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0098_491676a1de83.png\" />"
  },
